---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import DocCallout from "../../components/docs/DocCallout.astro";

const toc = [
  { title: "HTTP Server", href: "#http-server", depth: 2 },
  { title: "Core Routes", href: "#core-routes", depth: 2 },
  { title: "Mobile & Companion", href: "#mobile-companion", depth: 2 },
  { title: "Transport & Auth", href: "#transport-auth", depth: 2 },
  { title: "OpenAPI", href: "#openapi", depth: 2 },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Server & API"
  subtitle="Hono server composition in packages/nikcli/src/server/server.ts and packages/nikcli/src/server/routes."
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="http-server" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>HTTP Server</h2>
    <p>
      The server is implemented with Hono and SSE streaming. It exposes REST, event, companion,
      connector, and mobile APIs while resolving workspace context from request headers or query
      params before most handlers run.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="core-routes" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Core Routes</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Namespace</th>
          <th>Purpose</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>/global</code></td><td>Global runtime information and top-level helpers.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/project</code></td><td>Project metadata and discovery.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/pty</code></td><td>Pseudo-terminal and shell streaming endpoints.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/config</code></td><td>Config inspection and mutation helpers.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/experimental</code></td><td>Experimental APIs including workspace flows.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/session</code></td><td>Session CRUD, messages, share, and stream endpoints.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/permission</code></td><td>Permission prompt responses.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/question</code></td><td>Interactive question responses.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/provider</code></td><td>Provider catalog and model APIs.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/companion</code></td><td>Companion web UI endpoints.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/user</code></td><td>User auth and profile endpoints.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/mobile</code></td><td>Mobile app pairing, tokens, and session streaming.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/connectors</code></td><td>Connector configuration and auth flows.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/chatbot</code></td><td>Chat bot integrations and webhook flows.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/mcp</code></td><td>MCP server routes.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/tui</code></td><td>TUI-side control and session helpers.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/</code></td><td>Studio and file routes mounted at the root.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="mobile-companion" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Mobile & Companion</h2>
    <p>
      The server powers the browser companion UI, mobile session streaming, approval responses,
      repo import flows, and experimental workspace events in addition to the core CLI APIs.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="transport-auth" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>Transport & Auth</h2>
    <DocCallout type="info" title="Workspace context">
      <p>
        Most routes accept <code>x-nikcli-directory</code> or <code>x-nikcli-workspace</code> to
        resolve the active workspace before handling the request.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
    <p>
      The server supports CORS, optional basic auth, bearer flows for mobile and remote clients, and
      origin handling for localhost plus approved domains.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="openapi" class="mb-16 scroll-mt-24">
    <h2>OpenAPI</h2>
    <p>OpenAPI specs are exposed at <code>/doc</code> and generated with <code>@hono/zod-openapi</code>.</p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
